{"expires":1779742148718,"value":{"code":200,"headers":{"etag":"W/\"YaMan3ugcL\"","last-modified":"Mon, 25 May 2026 19:49:08 GMT","cache-control":"max-age=3600"},"body":{"title":"Deployment","slug":"deployment","tags":["deployment","production","hosting"],"content":"# Deployment\n\nThis guide covers deploying your app to production environments.\n\n## Build for Production\n\n```bash\nnpm run build\n```\n\nThe output is placed in `.output/`. It is a self-contained Node.js server.\n\n## Environment Variables\n\nSet environment variables on your hosting provider:\n\n| Variable | Description |\n|----------|-------------|\n| `NUXT_PUBLIC_APP_NAME` | Public app name |\n| `API_SECRET` | Server-side secret |\n| `DATABASE_URL` | Database connection string |\n\n## Hosting Options\n\n- **Vercel** — zero-config, push to deploy\n- **Fly.io** — Docker-based, good for full-stack\n- **Railway** — simple Postgres + Node bundles\n- **Self-hosted** — run `.output/server/index.mjs` behind nginx\n","body":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"element","tag":"h1","props":{"id":"deployment"},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Deployment"}]},{"type":"element","tag":"p","props":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"This guide covers deploying your app to production environments."}]},{"type":"element","tag":"h2","props":{"id":"build-for-production"},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Build for Production"}]},{"type":"element","tag":"pre","props":{"className":"language-bash","code":"npm run build\n","language":"bash","meta":"","style":"undefined"},"children":[{"type":"element","tag":"code","props":{"__ignoreMap":""},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"npm run build\n"}]}]},{"type":"element","tag":"p","props":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The output is placed in "},{"type":"element","tag":"code","props":{"className":[]},"children":[{"type":"text","value":".output/"}]},{"type":"text","value":". It is a self-contained Node.js server."}]},{"type":"element","tag":"h2","props":{"id":"envi